WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome.
-Did I sit too soon?

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:05.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, that was perfect.
Thank you.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just like Jim,
I met you at the Emmys,

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
or I saw you at the Emmys.
We had met before.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.342
Did you have a first time --

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:10.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congrats on the nomination,
first of all.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:13.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you as well.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:15.982 size:75% position:38%
Yes, it was my first
big Emmy experience.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was your first
Emmy experience.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´ve been to
the creative arts Emmys.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this one, it´s the mondo.
-This is the real D.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s the real -- the real D.
-Yeah.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I think I almost bumped
into you

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.726 size:75% position:38%
or knocked you over.
-No, no, not at all.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was salmon swimming
upstream, guys.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:29.696
-There was a lot of people.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.398
-There was a lot going on.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.532
Yeah, but it was really fun

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
until we had to go
and take the pictures.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Ann Dowd,
you go in front of me.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:38.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I love her.
And she´s lovely.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.807
-She was wonderful, won an Emmy.
Fantastic. Well-deserved.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well-deserved.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it´s just --
the people that you revere

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.245
and that you see and you
respect, and you´re like,

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.614
"I am two feet in front of them

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:50.250
or feeling their hot breath
on my neck, and that´s okay."

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-So, it´s great.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.888
-Oh, my God, all my favorites
and now we´re a little sweaty.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.123
And it´s a little hot.
And I don´t want to smell them.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.392
-Right. And we´re all equal.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I will say
if there was the one --

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:04.264 size:88% position:44%
The biggest star there,
for my money, was Oprah.

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you could tell everybody
wants to

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.635
kind of rub elbows with Oprah.
Everyone wants to say hello.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.936
You kind of hit the jackpot.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.638
You had already won the Emmys

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:13.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you had
lunch with Oprah.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and she --
-Yeah.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.344
-And this didn´t happen by
coincidence. She reached out.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, it was on purpose.
-She called you?

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.314 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah. She called me,

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:22.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I literally thought
I was being punk´d.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:24.484 size:78% position:39%
-I know that "Punk´d"
is not on anymore.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was like,
"is this Ashton?"

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:28.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you brought "Punk´d" back,
you would do it for that.

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:29.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For sure.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:32.392
Let´s punk Chrissy Metz,
thinking that Oprah called her.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:35.495
But yes, she just -- gratefully,
called me and asked me to lunch.

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:36.896 size:78% position:39%
And it was so lovely.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.833
Milo -- Sterling and I were
sitting next to each other.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then Milo and Ron,
and then of course

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.803
Susan and Chris and Mandy
were on the other side.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.271
But Oprah was, like, the middle.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we´re like, "Are you on the
right or left of Oprah?"

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right,
´cause that´s how it goes.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-Right.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yes,
the lunch was really lovely.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How quickly into
a lunch with Oprah

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:59.352
are you inspired in a way
that changes your life forever?

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You´re not joking.
About two seconds.

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:05.191
-Really?
-When she says "Hello, Chrissy."

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:08.595
I was like, "Okay. Okay."

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:12.165
And then I hug her and I´m like,
wow, your home is so beautiful,

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:14.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she stopped for a second
and she said,

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.269 size:84% position:42%
"You know what? It is."

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:19.038 size:81% position:41%
And it seems a little,
you´re like, "What?"

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
You might think
it´s pretentious.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.209
But it´s the most beautiful
thing because we don´t ever

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
relish and enjoy what we´ve
worked really hard for.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:27.447
And I thought that was so
beautiful that she stopped

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she just was like,
thank you for --

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, thanking me
for working really hard.

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:33.219
And I think that -- We all need
to do that more often.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s so great.
-So yeah, .2 seconds.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, for sure.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:37.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that´s --
I think when that was over,

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.359
she said, "Oh, I´ve lost a step.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:42.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m usually -- I´m usually
a little faster."

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:47.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this is -- this really
speaks to the crazy difference

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
in your show between year one
and year two,

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:50.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is obviously,
last year around this time,

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
you guys were
about to be married.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:52.639
You´d been working on the show.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:54.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
You knew you had
something special.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:58.878
But now, you are at "lunch with
Oprah" level as a cast.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:00.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
How has it felt --
-Where do I go from here?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.114
Is that what you´re asking?

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I guess,
in the way that Oprah

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:05.818
is appreciating her house,

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.654
are you guys all appreciating
where you´re at as a show?

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:08.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, for sure.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:11.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, last season, we were
like, "Please, dear God.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.293
Please.
Please somebody watch the show.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.328
I really hope you love it as
much as we love making it."

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now, you know,
I cry with people in bathrooms

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.432 size:78% position:39%
and in the chip aisle
at the grocery store.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.968
And so I´m like, "Okay, I think
we´re reaching people,"

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is so amazing

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.672
´cause that´s what everybody
wants to do with their art.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you ever,
even with all the success,

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:29.309
do you want to go back to a time
where you didn´t have to cry

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
with people in the bathroom?
Or is it worth it?

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it worth the trade-off?
-It´s totally worth it.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, good.
-And I love to cry, so...

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, good.
-It actually works out.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.284
-There are a lot of things,

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of elements of
the show I love.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:43.189
Personally, my favorite element
is that you´re a Steelers fan.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:44.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Stillers.
-Stillers.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.292
-No, I didn´t know that you
knew, but that´s Stillers.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, Pittsburghese.
-Yeah, Pittsburghese.

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I studied up on it.
-That´s good.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.965 size:78% position:39%
-I´m not great at it.
-That´s all right.

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:53.366 size:81% position:41%
-But I know it exists.

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:54.834
-But Stillers was -- that´s,
like, that´s level two at least.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, good.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:59.739
But you -- you did not have a
connection to that beforehand?

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:02.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. I mean, I grew up
in the South where, you know,

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:03.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
football is a religion, right?
-Yeah.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.245 size:75% position:38%
-So I love football.

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:07.447
But I have a lot of friends or
gentlemen who prefer gentlemen

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
so they don´t really watch
sports.

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-Right?

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:15.622
It´s fine, ´cause we do other
things together, which is great.

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
But when I go home,
I get to watch football

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I get to watch sports
with my family.

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:23.129
But I did love the Stillers when
I was younger, which is bizarre,

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:24.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause I had no connection
to them.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
They´re a loveable team.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:27.767
-They´re a loveable team.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.937
-I would imagine that Pittsburgh
has embraced the show

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.672
to a level that they probably

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
don´t usually embrace other
shows.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:38.177
And I think that we hopefully,
get to have a little trip there,

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe this season.
That would be super cool.

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:42.515
-It´s really fun, and it´s
a beautiful place to go.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you will really enjoy it.
And I just got to say

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:45.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
congratulations on the show,
Chrissy.

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s so wonderful.
-So grateful.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.621
-And just such a delight to talk
to you.

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:49.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.

